rfd: a native Haiku backend (BFilePanel, BAlert)

rfd has no Haiku backend (its xdg-portal and GTK3 ones are for Linux and the BSDs). Add one: the
Tracker's file panel for open (one or several files), pick folder and save, BAlert for message
dialogs, through a small C++ shim (src/backend/haiku/rfd_haiku.cpp) that build.rs compiles with the
target's C++ compiler (CXX_<target>/AR_<target>, as the cc crate reads them; no new dependency, so
Cargo.lock stays as it is) and links with libtracker, libbe and libstdc++.

- The panels and alerts are windows of the program's BApplication, which the backend never makes:
  a winit program gets one from Haiku's in-process Wayland server (wayland-server-inproc.so creates
  it when the client connects and casts be_app to its own class later, so a second one must not
  exist). Without be_app a file dialog returns None and a message dialog the answer that changes
  nothing, noted on standard error.
- Filters: the panel has no type menu, so all filters are merged into one BRefFilter (extension in
  any letter case; folders always shown; "*" shows everything).
- With a parent window the panel is app-modal. The panel's answer goes to a BLooper of the shim;
  B_CANCEL, which the panel sends whenever it hides (after an answer too), ends the wait.
- Sync calls block the calling thread; the async ones wait on a thread of their own and resolve
  through rfd's oneshot channel.
- A program exiting with a dialog open: an exit handler (registered with the first dialog, so it
  runs before libbe's static destructors) locks the open dialogs' loopers and suspends their
  threads while they wait; else a message reaching one after exit() freed libbe's looper list
  crashes its thread in BLooperList::FindLooperPred. A dialog closing then leaves its loopers alone.

Replaces the earlier stub (every dialog cancelled). Photocraft phase P4. Applies with -p1 to rfd 0.17.2.

